{"title":"2023 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the following arrangement of positive integers.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The 1st row includes the odd integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the 2nd row includes the two even integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th row\n</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: circle\">\n<li>begins with the integer that is one more than the last integer in the previous row,</li>\n<li>begins with the integer that is one more than the last integer in the previous row,</li>\n<li>includes, in increasing order, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive odd integers when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd, and</li>\n<li>includes, in increasing order, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive even integers when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is even.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A useful fact about this arrangement is that the integer in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th row and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th position (that is, the last position in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th row) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00ff2fd800eb5e3300360954f5880cd34273bee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e9136809f832318fdd66a5180d0e20660e072b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{2} = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> and 16 is the integer in the 4th position of the 4th row.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the average of the integers in the 5th row?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the last number in the 4th row is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and each row begins with the integer that is one more than the last integer in the previous row, the first number in the 5th row is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/8562e5012440817ee7b4fbcbe37d1b0811806871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 + 1 = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Using the fact that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th row for all odd rows where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> contains only odd consecutive numbers, we find that the rest of the numbers are:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0d041c1be848b62c75c26fa3c63a285277c7ffb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 + 2 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/06899a2bcfd7627ec8fe4ecde0f3e18f13b1649e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 + 2 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69d1ab37a4f36b857893e4dd0ba3248fba942de0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 + 2 = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c9c63fd97cb6c6a32797ee5e2cc376c8808989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 + 2 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>The average of the numbers in the 5th row is then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cfd9bee77fc965943f4d087e68e8257cde74ac8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{17 + 19 + 21 + 23 + 25}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"38\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/4008ed756ef1ca1265e3b882bdaf501890397f48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36 + 44 + 25}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/674210acfc0818aa88ea8bfb6da7b79b40991f6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{105}{5} = \\boxed{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the fact that the last number of the 5th row must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1cb2b1216f6a5a6e9672c52b9cbe9349231f450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2} = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />. Since the numbers are all consecutive odd integers, we have see that the previous numbers are:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac4df4463efe7f685589c5017c787918811aaee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 - 2 = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f14b5b8d13f2c86325946c830618f47ea4b24f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 - 2 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb351cd8c518d04aecec1668354b66178c4a32c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 - 2 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb31c48611ee89ca67a3b48cd02708e48c0999de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 - 2 = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Using the same process as solution 1 at the end, we see that the average of the numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/3866dbf1d954e409beb13f52f7ed7618bedc183f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the same process as solution 1 or 2 until we find that the middle number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Since the numbers have the same common difference from each other and there are an odd number of numbers, the median must be equal to the average of the numbers.\n</p><p>Thus, the average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/3866dbf1d954e409beb13f52f7ed7618bedc183f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018023516\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 156/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1994/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5873/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   23.936      1 2023_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%   23.936      1 -total\n 21.76%    5.209      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35535:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018023516 and revision id 277860. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}